{"duration_api_ms":2152913,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"43fb5533-258a-43cc-836e-7c71093a2488","total_cost_usd":3.014475599999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":138,"cache_creation_input_tokens":143178,"cache_read_input_tokens":7935143,"output_tokens":85031,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":143178,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2775,"cache_read_input_tokens":158979,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1223},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4069,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004149,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":138,"outputTokens":85031,"cacheReadInputTokens":7935143,"cacheCreationInputTokens":143178,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.010326599999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":8129,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":98,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured PostgreSQL 16 streaming replication across node1 (primary), node2 and node3 (standbys), with all replication traffic carried over TLS and mutual-cert authentication enforced via a cluster-dedicated CA. Verified live data replication, rejection of a cert not issued by the CA, and full recovery of all three nodes after sequential restarts with proven boot-identity changes.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed PostgreSQL 16 on node1, node2, node3\",\"Generated a dedicated CA on node1 (/etc/postgresql-ca/ca.key+ca.crt) and issued CA-signed server certs (CN=node1/node2/node3) plus a client cert (CN=replicator) for mutual TLS\",\"Distributed CA cert, server certs/keys, and replicator client cert/key to /etc/postgresql/16/main/tls on each node (outside the data directory, owned by postgres, 600 perms on keys) via secret_env-passed base64\",\"Configured postgresql.conf on all nodes: listen_addresses='*', ssl=on with CA-signed cert/key/ca file paths, wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10, hot_standby=on\",\"Configured pg_hba.conf on all nodes to require hostssl + cert clientcert=verify-full for replication connections restricted to the cluster subnet, removing the prior scram-sha-256 replication rules\",\"Created the REPLICATION role 'replicator' on node1\",\"Created physical replication slots node2_slot/node3_slot on node1 to guard against WAL recycling\",\"Bootstrapped node2 and node3 via pg_basebackup over sslmode=verify-full using the replicator client cert, with -R to auto-generate primary_conninfo/standby.signal\",\"Diagnosed and fixed a key/cert mismatch on node3 (caused by an earlier base64 copy error) by restoring the correct server.key and replicator.key, verified via matching RSA modulus\",\"Started both standbys and confirmed pg_stat_replication on node1 shows node2 and node3 streaming with ssl=t and client_dn=/CN=replicator\",\"Verified live replication by inserting rows on node1 and confirming visibility on node2 and node3, then cleaned up test tables\",\"Proved CA enforcement: a locally-generated self-signed cert with CN=replicator was rejected by node1 with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca'\",\"Captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, service state, recovery state, replication state) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2, then node3, then node1 (primary) one at a time via 'shutdown -r now', polled until each came back, and proved each node's /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id changed\",\"After each restart, verified PostgreSQL was active, standbys resumed streaming over TLS with client_dn=/CN=replicator, and re-verified end-to-end data replication after all three nodes were back up\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"PostgreSQL streaming replication with node1 as writable primary, node2/node3 as standbys\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d6e4bbf713034b33\",\"cmd-9368f2f8cb6c4987\",\"cmd-dcf701ad08454fef\",\"cmd-e84ca458d8db4fb7\",\"cmd-2834d4f4f6ad4a3b\",\"cmd-0e0f55071b554d96\",\"cmd-da9f47f54e534fe2\",\"cmd-e595a43446264c53\",\"cmd-a24ce7b54c4345d0\"],\"summary\":\"replicator role created on node1; node2/node3 bootstrapped via pg_basebackup with -R; both show pg_is_in_recovery=t and appear in pg_stat_replication as 'streaming'; an inserted row on node1 was visible on both standbys\"},{\"requirement\":\"CA created for the cluster and used to sign server/client certificates\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e97d92ff61554368\",\"cmd-ec21b05d11994ff7\"],\"summary\":\"openssl req -x509 created ca.key/ca.crt on node1; per-node server certs (CN=node1/node2/node3) and a replicator client cert were all signed by this CA (CAcreateserial)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Replication traffic carried over TLS\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3059a9abe73a4115\",\"cmd-cad12c4d0d904624\",\"cmd-0e0f55071b554d96\",\"cmd-a36112bdbe5c411e\"],\"summary\":\"postgresql.conf ssl=on with CA-signed cert/key on all nodes; SHOW ssl returns 'on'; pg_stat_replication joined with pg_stat_ssl shows ssl=t and cipher TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 for both standby connections, including after the primary's restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Replication connections accepted only from peers presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0b97bba284064a2a\",\"cmd-0e0f55071b554d96\",\"cmd-1d9108c4031d4450\",\"cmd-ffecea699c3747a5\"],\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf requires hostssl+cert clientcert=verify-full for replication; legitimate connections show client_dn=/CN=replicator; a locally generated self-signed cert (not CA-issued) was rejected by node1 with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca'\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4b741eb6d12541ad\",\"cmd-cfcd9d5a073b4f12\",\"cmd-bc135f148ab040c6\",\"cmd-a36112bdbe5c411e\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id dfeb3b70...; reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; post-reboot boot_id e4d99bb9... (changed); postgresql active, not in recovery, ssl=on, both standbys reconnected streaming over TLS\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1735b79ef58f4b7c\",\"cmd-d8e8b1ebeeda4d56\",\"cmd-8919be36aaa34a8b\",\"cmd-8c42c8ef1c2c49cb\",\"cmd-40e37f2c20554af1\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id a0c36ad2...; reboot acknowledged then connection reset; post-reboot boot_id d9690708... (changed); postgresql active, still in recovery, small replay lag, node1 shows node2 streaming again over TLS\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-edfe87f962b6494c\",\"cmd-5fcc9e88aa124550\",\"cmd-1f826c4f2ab74b60\",\"cmd-42ea411c40534b8d\",\"cmd-833839105cb9450d\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id e8afb731...; reboot acknowledged then connection timeout; post-reboot boot_id cd39558c... (changed); postgresql active, still in recovery, small replay lag, node1 shows node3 streaming again over TLS\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart data/cluster health verified end-to-end across all three nodes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4436c44f72414597\",\"cmd-56980d75fb064f87\",\"cmd-6ab6db6567c34180\",\"cmd-77695af7b7954a97\"],\"summary\":\"After all three nodes were restarted, a new row inserted on node1 was confirmed present on both node2 and node3, then the test table was dropped\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured PostgreSQL 16 streaming replication across node1 (primary), node2 and node3 (standbys), with all replication traffic carried over TLS and mutual-cert authentication enforced via a cluster-dedicated CA. Verified live data replication, rejection of a cert not issued by the CA, and full recovery of all three nodes after sequential restarts with proven boot-identity changes.","actions_performed":["Installed PostgreSQL 16 on node1, node2, node3","Generated a dedicated CA on node1 (/etc/postgresql-ca/ca.key+ca.crt) and issued CA-signed server certs (CN=node1/node2/node3) plus a client cert (CN=replicator) for mutual TLS","Distributed CA cert, server certs/keys, and replicator client cert/key to /etc/postgresql/16/main/tls on each node (outside the data directory, owned by postgres, 600 perms on keys) via secret_env-passed base64","Configured postgresql.conf on all nodes: listen_addresses='*', ssl=on with CA-signed cert/key/ca file paths, wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10, hot_standby=on","Configured pg_hba.conf on all nodes to require hostssl + cert clientcert=verify-full for replication connections restricted to the cluster subnet, removing the prior scram-sha-256 replication rules","Created the REPLICATION role 'replicator' on node1","Created physical replication slots node2_slot/node3_slot on node1 to guard against WAL recycling","Bootstrapped node2 and node3 via pg_basebackup over sslmode=verify-full using the replicator client cert, with -R to auto-generate primary_conninfo/standby.signal","Diagnosed and fixed a key/cert mismatch on node3 (caused by an earlier base64 copy error) by restoring the correct server.key and replicator.key, verified via matching RSA modulus","Started both standbys and confirmed pg_stat_replication on node1 shows node2 and node3 streaming with ssl=t and client_dn=/CN=replicator","Verified live replication by inserting rows on node1 and confirming visibility on node2 and node3, then cleaned up test tables","Proved CA enforcement: a locally-generated self-signed cert with CN=replicator was rejected by node1 with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca'","Captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, service state, recovery state, replication state) on all three nodes","Restarted node2, then node3, then node1 (primary) one at a time via 'shutdown -r now', polled until each came back, and proved each node's /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id changed","After each restart, verified PostgreSQL was active, standbys resumed streaming over TLS with client_dn=/CN=replicator, and re-verified end-to-end data replication after all three nodes were back up"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"PostgreSQL streaming replication with node1 as writable primary, node2/node3 as standbys","command_ids":["cmd-d6e4bbf713034b33","cmd-9368f2f8cb6c4987","cmd-dcf701ad08454fef","cmd-e84ca458d8db4fb7","cmd-2834d4f4f6ad4a3b","cmd-0e0f55071b554d96","cmd-da9f47f54e534fe2","cmd-e595a43446264c53","cmd-a24ce7b54c4345d0"],"summary":"replicator role created on node1; node2/node3 bootstrapped via pg_basebackup with -R; both show pg_is_in_recovery=t and appear in pg_stat_replication as 'streaming'; an inserted row on node1 was visible on both standbys"},{"requirement":"CA created for the cluster and used to sign server/client certificates","command_ids":["cmd-e97d92ff61554368","cmd-ec21b05d11994ff7"],"summary":"openssl req -x509 created ca.key/ca.crt on node1; per-node server certs (CN=node1/node2/node3) and a replicator client cert were all signed by this CA (CAcreateserial)"},{"requirement":"Replication traffic carried over TLS","command_ids":["cmd-3059a9abe73a4115","cmd-cad12c4d0d904624","cmd-0e0f55071b554d96","cmd-a36112bdbe5c411e"],"summary":"postgresql.conf ssl=on with CA-signed cert/key on all nodes; SHOW ssl returns 'on'; pg_stat_replication joined with pg_stat_ssl shows ssl=t and cipher TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 for both standby connections, including after the primary's restart"},{"requirement":"Replication connections accepted only from peers presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA","command_ids":["cmd-0b97bba284064a2a","cmd-0e0f55071b554d96","cmd-1d9108c4031d4450","cmd-ffecea699c3747a5"],"summary":"pg_hba.conf requires hostssl+cert clientcert=verify-full for replication; legitimate connections show client_dn=/CN=replicator; a locally generated self-signed cert (not CA-issued) was rejected by node1 with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca'"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-4b741eb6d12541ad","cmd-cfcd9d5a073b4f12","cmd-bc135f148ab040c6","cmd-a36112bdbe5c411e"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id dfeb3b70...; reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; post-reboot boot_id e4d99bb9... (changed); postgresql active, not in recovery, ssl=on, both standbys reconnected streaming over TLS"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-1735b79ef58f4b7c","cmd-d8e8b1ebeeda4d56","cmd-8919be36aaa34a8b","cmd-8c42c8ef1c2c49cb","cmd-40e37f2c20554af1"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id a0c36ad2...; reboot acknowledged then connection reset; post-reboot boot_id d9690708... (changed); postgresql active, still in recovery, small replay lag, node1 shows node2 streaming again over TLS"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-edfe87f962b6494c","cmd-5fcc9e88aa124550","cmd-1f826c4f2ab74b60","cmd-42ea411c40534b8d","cmd-833839105cb9450d"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id e8afb731...; reboot acknowledged then connection timeou